{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"30e8e41e5ab44c4e1c92faebc0aa2a6ead56ffc0a63dbf3043d95b85ca2a94ea","digest":{"component_or_area":"CI module-size gate (gerrit-verify.yaml, test.yml)","key_entities":[".github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml",".github/workflows/test.yml",".github/module-size-allowlist.txt","listed=","grep -vE","awk","tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py","reconcile.py"],"problem_keywords":["module-size gate","empty allowlist","grep exit code","shell error handling","ci workflow"],"propositions":["The module-size gate step exits with code 1 when the allowlist is empty (zero non-comment entries) because grep returns 1 on no match, triggering bash -e pipefail abort before the over-cap check runs.","The listed= assignment in both gerrit-verify.yaml and test.yml must be wrapped with a guard (|| true) to tolerate grep returning 1 on empty allowlist.","The gate must complete successfully with exit 0 and print 'Module-size gate: OK' when run against a comment-only allowlist with no over-cap files.","The gate must still fail (exit 1) when a non-allow-listed file exceeds 800 LOC, preserving existing rejection behavior for the non-empty case."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787721854623767001,"uuid":"8db584e0-2e74-4328-a5bc-d325d4fae1d9"}